### Import path breaking change (6.0.0)

Source: https://github.com/resend/react-email/blob/canary/apps/docs/getting-started/updating-react-email.mdx

All components and rendering utilities were unified into the react-email package. Imports from @react-email/components or individual component packages must be changed to imports from react-email.

```typescript
import { Button, Html, Head, render } from "@react-email/components"; // [!code --]
import { Button, Html, Head, render } from "react-email"; // [!code ++]
```

### CLI > F.A.Q > How can I define props specific to the email's preview?

Source: https://github.com/resend/react-email/blob/canary/apps/docs/cli.mdx

To define default props for your email preview, you can attach a PreviewProps object to your exported React component. When the preview server renders the email, it will automatically use these properties as the component props.

